WEBVTT

NOTE Hit Your Mark introduction. English captions.

1
00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.980
Three. Two. One. Hit your mark.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.450
First, the stage. Say he walks
at the same speed the whole way.

3
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.890
Every second, he gets three quarters
of a meter closer to the mark.

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.870
Next, the pool. The swimmer pushes
off the wall and keeps the same speed.

5
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.240
Every second, the swimmer gets one and
a half meters farther from the start.

6
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.990
One distance goes down. The other goes up.

7
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.820
But they're both straight lines.

8
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.540
The slope is the rate. That's how much
the distance changes every second.

9
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.770
The y-intercept is where the line hits
the y-axis, right at zero seconds.

10
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.780
He starts six meters from the mark. The
swimmer starts three meters from the wall.

11
00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.040
That's where you are
when the clock starts.

12
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.370
Change either one, and
the whole line moves.

13
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.650
Now, here's the problem.

14
00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.660
The director wants him there sooner.

15
00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:52.620
The coach wants a faster swim.

16
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.290
Stick with the old plan, and you'll miss.

17
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.030
So what do you change?
The rate, or the start?

18
00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:02.880
You'll do both. The stage
first, then the pool.

19
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.980
Graph it, adjust it, and hit your mark.
